# What the performer brings, not what the repo ships. The recordings are
# somebody's takes and set.json is their arrangement -- live pot positions
# included, so it would churn on every single commit. The system patterns in
# pattern/system/ stay tracked: those are the instrument.
pattern/user/
pattern/set.json
pattern/current.json
pattern/sessions/
# The clips that reach the performer's own takes. The factory clips beside them
# are the instrument and stay tracked; these are somebody's evening on it, like
# the takes themselves. They share a folder only until the folders are split
# into a fixed factory tree and a movable user one -- see
# .claude/notes/2026-09-04-clip-und-session-dateien.md, step 4 -- after which
# this pattern-match can go.
# The presets a performer generates and keeps. Default.json is the instrument's
# and is tracked; the rest come out of a3-clip-gen and are somebody's taste.
pattern/clips/*.json
!pattern/clips/Default.json

